WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.697
Now we combine the two halves of the module.

00:00:02.697 --> 00:00:07.977
A realistic preparation query often cleans text and transforms time in the same result.

00:00:07.977 --> 00:00:14.457
We will normalize the patient name, extract an email domain, reduce the admission timestamp to month grain,

00:00:14.457 --> 00:00:16.332
and calculate length of stay.

00:00:16.332 --> 00:00:20.197
The key is that each transformation has a clear purpose.

00:00:20.197 --> 00:00:23.742
For this activity, make a prediction before you run anything.

00:00:23.742 --> 00:00:26.362
State what one output row should represent, which records you expect to remain,

00:00:26.362 --> 00:00:31.267
and what edge case is most likely to expose a mistake.

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:34.607
Then run the SQL and compare the result with that prediction.

00:00:34.607 --> 00:00:40.462
If it does not match, debug the logic in small pieces instead of changing several clauses at once.

00:00:40.462 --> 00:00:45.837
This is the same habit you would use in a real analytics project: validate the meaning of the result,

00:00:45.837 --> 00:00:47.837
not only whether the statement executes.
